Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillet: a walked end cut by the face at the end runs on over the flat
stretch beyond a curved wall, over the curved wall's own surface continued
in a span of its own (mitcad#1926, mitcad#1987).

A concave rounding along a fin's foot, its chain ending where the fin's
sloping top runs down to the plate: the fin's side is a curved wall (an
extrusion of a B-spline curve) bending tangentially into a flat stretch
(a plane) lower than the radius. The contact left the curved wall across
its edge with the top (the face at the end, holding the spine's end
vertex), and the walk ran on over the wall's surface past the flat
stretch's edge, the curve's polynomial continued; it stopped 1.2 mm short
of the end, and WalkedCutToEnd's walk on from there, over a face of N's
surface bounded at the curve's ends, failed.

- ChFi3d_RunOnSurface (new): where N is an extrusion whose basis curve
  ends at an edge J of N across which a plane N2 (neither Fo nor B) goes
  on tangentially to N, holding J's tangent line, N's surface with the
  basis curve continued past J by the polynomial of its span at J, in a
  span of its own (N's parameters kept on N; J's knot removed where the
  two are one polynomial), as long as its tangent stays within 45 degrees
  of J's. Past J it bends in from N2's plane as the curve went on bending,
  the way the bodies stored in reported designs run such a rounding on
  (mitcad#1987: N2's plane, this patch's first form, left the rounding up
  to 0.45 mm out at the flat stretch's far end, 0.5 mm3 at each arm).
- WalkedCutToEnd: the walk on over such a surface on a face of it bounded
  in v too (N's v range widened by the spine's length both ways), so that
  a walk reaching its ends stops at edges with vertices.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece: at an end given as such (a point where the cut
  meets the other contact) no section bounds the cut, which may reach
  past that point's section (where the other contact turns in towards the
  face beyond): the cut is kept in the piece on its other side only.
- WalkedCutToEnd: with such a surface, the blend is walked again from
  the end piece's other end (as for a tight tangent face at the end) and
  cut by the face at the end from the crossing on; where the other
  contact meets the line of the edge Eq between the other face and the
  face at the end only past the spine's end vertex, on both surfaces,
  Eq is prolonged there and the face at the end grows up to the cut (as
  ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd does); the flat stretch, wholly under the blend,
  has its edges cut at its vertices so that the builder drops it, and its
  edges with the face at the end are passed as cut edges. Also where the
  walk ran on past the spine's end.
- PerformSetOfSurf: an end try that fails (its inner walk) no longer
  leaves the stripe failed: done is restored, as the comment there says.
- WalkedCutToEnd's pieces in the history: the walked piece that takes
  the end piece's place, and the piece cut by the face at the end, are
  faces generated by the spine's edges the end piece was (myEVIMap, as
  the other patches that replace pieces keep it); Generated() left their
  faces out, so that they had no name of their own and a later rounding
  along the top's edge with them found no edge.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_wall_run_on.cpp, test_reported_body
(ctest geometry.fillet_wall_run_on): on the stored case
`fillet-wall-run-on` of MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES, the outer foot rounded with
3 by OCCT's fillet alone: valid, the flat stretches gone, the foot on the
plate that of a ball on the plate and the curved side continued by its
polynomial within 0.01 mm, the volume a little under the run-on over the
flat stretch's plane (by at most a twentieth of the material added);
documented to fail without this patch.
No synthetic body: a U of cubic B-spline sides went another way at its
ends (invalid with and without the patch). It fails without the patch
(shown 2026-11-20 by tools/occt-port-proof.py).

Failures (mitcad#1986): the longer B-spline curve's construction fails
with OCCT's reports of a computation it cannot make
(ChFi3d_IsComputationFailure, 0016): that end is not run on. Any other
failure (a broken invariant, a signal) is rethrown.
